-- hy-locked: an action done with the write lock held, so that one writer at a time renders a module,
-- records it, checks it and writes its versions (Avik, 2026-11-21: "multiple threads writing to store
-- at once and it dropping content": every write went through one scratch file and recorded a whole
-- module, with no lock). Without the lock nothing is done (part of language-implementation-remainder)
hy-locked : Proc W Unit → Proc W Unit
hy-locked act = bind hy-lock (λ fd → if wlt fd #9223372036854775808 then act else h-fail "hyperactive: the write lock could not be taken; nothing was written")
